  "notes": "こぼれる describes something spilling out or overflowing from a container, often accidentally.\n\nTRANSITIVITY:\n- Type: ⟦{自動詞|じどうし}→自動詞：10977_jidoushi⟧ (intransitive)\n- Pair: ⟦こぼす→こぼす：02104_kobosu⟧ (transitive, to spill something)\n\nASPECT (こぼれている):\nIndicates the resulting state: ⟦{水|みず}→水：02258_mizu⟧⟦が→が：00051_ga⟧こぼれて⟦いる→いる：00495_iru⟧ means 'water has spilled' (state).\n\nCOMMON PATTERNS:\n- ⟦{水|みず}→水：02258_mizu⟧⟦が→が：00051_ga⟧こぼれる: water spills\n- ⟦{涙|なみだ}→涙：02235_namida⟧⟦が→が：00051_ga⟧こぼれる: tears fall/overflow\n- ⟦{笑|え}み→笑み：13768_emi⟧⟦が→が：00051_ga⟧こぼれる: to break into a smile (figurative)\n- ⟦{光|ひかり}→光：01707_hikari⟧⟦が→が：00051_ga⟧こぼれる: light filters through\n\nWRITING:\nSometimes written as {零|こぼ}れる, though hiragana is more common.",
